Algorithm
Step 1: Start the program.
Step 2: Read the number of vertices and edges.
Step 3: Create an adjacency list to represent the graph.
Step 4: Enter the edges connecting the vertices.
Step 5: Accept the starting vertex from the user.
Step 6: Initialize all vertices as unvisited and set their BFS levels to -1.
Step 7: Mark the starting vertex as visited, set its BFS level to 0, and insert it into the queue.
Step 8: Remove a vertex from the queue and display it in the BFS traversal order.
Step 9: Check all adjacent vertices. If an adjacent vertex is unvisited, mark it as visited, calculate its BFS level, and insert it into the queue.
Step 10: Repeat Steps 8 and 9 until the queue becomes empty.
Step 11: Display all reachable vertices and identify the unvisited vertices.
Step 12: Count the reachable vertices and display the BFS level of each reachable vertex.
Step 13: Stop the program.
